x02-rng-alignment patch 09-creation-draws (git apply ignores this header)

E7 item: (i) the random-number stream, the creation draws: the two rand() values SAGE26 consumes and
discards each time it creates a galaxy. A measurement instrument, not a proposal for Mimic.

SAGE26 behaviour: init_galaxy (R/src/model_misc.c:65-201) calls (void)rand(); twice (R/src/model_misc.c:91-92)
and discards both, so each galaxy creation advances the process-global libc stream by two. init_galaxy is
called once per FoF evolution at most: in join_galaxies_of_progenitors when the FoF's cumulative galaxy
count is still zero after its first halo's progenitors (R/src/core_build_model.c:347-349).

Mimic behaviour replaced: Mimic creates a galaxy in init_new_halo (src/core/inheritance.c:97-107 at
the launch base, :109-125 after x01's series), called once from inherit_descendant_halos when the FoF
central's subhalo slice is empty (src/core/inheritance.c:186-188 at the launch base, :214-216 after the
series), and consumes no random number there.

What the patch changes: two discarded calls, (void)rand(); (void)rand();, as the first statements of
init_new_halo in src/core/inheritance.c, and #include <stdlib.h> in that file, which the build needs
(without it inheritance.c fails with "call to undeclared function 'rand'"). Nothing else. Nothing
consumes the stream between a FoF's creation and its classifier, so the calls' position inside
init_new_halo does not change the stream. With the package's keyed draw in place (no 08), no
production code reads the stream, so this patch alone must leave every galaxy unchanged (the null
control).

Predecessor: the launch base 5e91c80866cedb56a23fb8e53d23bb775f40269d with x01's seven series patches
applied in order from a3063d5836ebe86bfe5c96e4cc7fcd27fe177aa1 (01-particle-mass, 02-cosmic-time,
03-written-dt, 04-substep-count, 05-float-halo-state, 06-inheritance-resets,
07-written-halo-values-stacked); the hunk's context is x01 05-float-halo-state's init_new_halo, so the
patch needs 05 (rules section 6 variant otherwise). It applies with or without 08-cgm-useful-draw.patch.

Reading for i02: init_new_halo is core code shared by every package and both drivers (its caller
inherit_descendant_halos is called from src/core/build_model.c:400 and src/core/horizontal_driver.c:1142).
The calls only advance libc's stream; no production code in src/ or models/ calls rand() (the
generator-call search at the launch base), so sage16's and halos-only's output would not change,
unless a linked library reads the same stream. Under the horizontal driver the draws are consumed in
that driver's creation order, which differs from SAGE26's; they matter only together with a consumer
such as patch 08.

